  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Adapters own the mess",
      "items": [
        "Every vendor read lives behind one UsageProvider actor",
        "Each adapter declares Fidelity so a guess is never shown as official",
        "Sources/Providers is 40% of the app by line count"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One store, two consumers",
      "items": [
        "UsageStore is the only owner of snapshots and order",
        "Notch and Settings read the same ordered list so they cannot disagree",
        "UsageArchive keeps the last good reading across launches"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Activity is separate from usage",
      "items": [
        "Session monitors answer \"is it still working?\", not \"how much is left?\"",
        "Their only input to the store is isBusy, which sets polling cadence",
        "PhoneLink is built but switched off at the source (isAvailable = false)"
      ]
    }
  ]
